{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2keRQVo3g8TBLCzASr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`contacts.dedupe` now merges all three reported cases. `tests/test_dedupe.py` passes, and I didn't touch the test.\n\n**Root causes** (all in `name_key` in `contacts/dedupe.py`):\n\n1. **Incomplete accent table.** Only a handful of letters were stripped, so `ú` in \"Núñez\" survived and the names never matched. This is the reproduction in the test.\n2. **No Unicode normalization.** Mac input often arrives decomposed (`e` + combining acute), which never matches the precomposed `é` from Windows. The old code didn't normalize at all.\n3. **`ß` vs `ss`.** `.lower()` doesn't fold `ß`, so \"Straße\" and \"STRASSE\" stayed different. `casefold()` maps `ß` to `ss`.\n\n**Fix:** `name_key` now casefolds, applies NFKD, drops combining marks, and collapses whitespace. The accent table is gone, so any accented letter reduces to its base letter. `email_key` now uses `casefold()` too, for consistency.\n\n**Survivor order:** unchanged. `dedupe` still keeps the first-seen record.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `pytest tests`: 1 passed.\n- Ad hoc run with `Straße` / `STRASSE`, precomposed `José Müller` / decomposed `Jose\\u0301 Mu\\u0308ller`, and a non-breaking-space name variant. Survivors were the first of each group, as expected.\n\nI didn't commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit. The only file changed is `contacts/dedupe.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18759,"cache_read_input_tokens":49917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18759},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c4457e1-8cc8-4703-a362-8fe548329ee0","uuid":"0de01486-ae4f-4a